BT /F2 17 Tf 72 720 Td (2 Setting up) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 72 681 Td (2.1 Pairing the sensor) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 645 Td (2.1.1 First pairing) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 619 Td (Put the batteries in the outdoor sensor first and in the display second. The display) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 604 Td (searches for three minutes and shows a steady aerial symbol when it has found the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 589 Td (sensor.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 557 Td (2.1.2 Adding a second sensor) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 531 Td (Press and hold the CHANNEL button on the display for five seconds until the channel) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 516 Td (number flashes, then press the small RESET button inside the battery cover of the new) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 501 Td (sensor. The display gives it the next free channel, up to channel 3.) Tj ET
BT /F2 14 Tf 72 469 Td (2.2 Setting the alarms) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 441 Td (Each alarm watches one reading and sounds when that reading crosses its threshold. Press) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 426 Td (ALARM to choose an alarm, then press the up and down buttons to change its threshold.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 394 Td (2.2.1 Frost alarm) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 368 Td (This alarm sounds when the outdoor temperature falls to the threshold or below.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 72 336 Td (2.2.1.1 Choosing the threshold) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 311 Td (For most gardens, set this threshold to 4, which leaves you time to cover young plants) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 296 Td (before the night gets any colder. A higher value sounds the alarm on many nights that) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 281 Td (turn out to be mild.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 247 Td (WARNING: Never mount the outdoor sensor during a storm, and never climb a ladder in high wind.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 234 Td (Keep the mounting pole at least 3 metres away from overhead power lines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 760 Td (Skylark WS-3 Home Weather Station: User Manual) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 40 Td (Page 2 of 7) Tj ET
endstream
