BT /F2 13 Tf 72 394 Td (4.1.1 Rain funnel) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 368 Td (Clean it once a month in autumn, when falling leaves can block it. Lift it off, brush) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 353 Td (out the mesh with the brush from the box, and rinse it in clean water before you put it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 338 Td (back.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 306 Td (4.1.2 Solar panel) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 280 Td (Wipe it with a damp cloth every three months. It powers a small fan that keeps air) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 265 Td (moving past the temperature probe, so a dirty panel makes the temperature read high on) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 250 Td (sunny days.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 216 Td (WARNING: Never mount the outdoor sensor during a storm, and never climb a ladder in high wind.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 72 203 Td (Keep the mounting pole at least 3 metres away from overhead power lines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 760 Td (Skylark WS-3 Home Weather Station: User Manual) Tj ET
